      "source": [
        "## Glorot\n",
        "def DenseLayer_Glorot_tanh(n_in: int, n_out: int):\n",
        "  std = sqrt(2 / (n_in + n_out)) # Glorot + tanh: alpha=1\n",
        "  return DenseLayer(n_in, n_out, lambda x: x.tanh(), initializer = NormalInitializer(mean=0.0, std=std))\n",
        "\n",
        "## He\n",
        "def DenseLayer_He_relu(n_in: int, n_out: int):\n",
        "  std = sqrt(2 / n_in) # He + ReLU: alpha=2\n",
        "  return DenseLayer(n_in, n_out, lambda x: x.relu(), initializer = NormalInitializer(mean=0.0, std=std))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "To test the 2 intializers numerically, we would create 2 separate FFNN's with some sufficient amount of hidden layers and neurons, e.g. 10 layers and 100 neurons. The FFNN's would each have their own initialization, so one has Glorot initializer with the tanh activaiton function and the other would have the He initializer and ReLU activation function. Then we would complete a forward- and backwardpass through the network and then plot the variance of the activations and gradiants at each layer. Lastly, we would look at the plot and confirm that the variance stayed consistent and didn't explode or diminish."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Exercise j) Forward pass unit test\n",
        "\n",
        "Write a bit of code to make a unit test that the forward pass works. This can be done by defining a simple network with for example all weights equal to one (using the ConstantInitializer method) and identity activation functions.\n",
        "\n",
        "Hints: Use the [assert](https://www.w3schools.com/python/ref_keyword_assert.asp), the nparray_to_Var and the Var_to_nparray commands."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 147,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "k0miqRUAFtHl"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Output: [5. 5.]\n",
            "Test passed!\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# create Denselayer\n",
        "layer = DenseLayer(\n",
        "    n_in=2,\n",
        "    n_out=2,\n",
        "    act_fn=lambda x: x.identity(),\n",
        "    initializer=ConstantInitializer()\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# input\n",
        "x = nparray_to_Var(np.array([2.0, 3.0]))\n",
        "x = [item[0] for item in x] # convert to flat list\n",
        "\n",
        "# foward pass\n",
        "output = layer.forward(x)\n",
        "output = np.array([item.v for item in output]) #convert to numpy array\n",
        "print(\"Output:\", output)\n",
        "assert np.allclose(output, [5, 5]) # validate output with expected result\n",
        "print(\"Test passed!\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "faCxhfFnFtHp"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Loss functions\n",
        "\n",
        "We are only missing a loss function to we need to define a loss function and its derivative with respect to the output of the neural network $y$"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 148,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "I2eDYKvAFtHq"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def squared_loss(t, y):\n",
        "\n",
        "  # add check that sizes agree\n",
        "\n",
        "  def squared_loss_single(t, y):\n",
        "    Loss = Var(0.0)\n",
        "    for i in range(len(t)): # sum over outputs\n",
        "      Loss += (t[i]-y[i]) ** 2\n",
        "    return Loss\n",
        "\n",
        "  Loss = Var(0.0)\n",
        "  for n in range(len(t)): # sum over training data\n",
        "    Loss += squared_loss_single(t[n],y[n])\n",
        "  return Loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "SrwSJ2UWFtHu"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Exercise k) Implement cross entropy loss\n",
        "\n",
        "Insert code below to implement cross-entropy loss for general dimensionality of $t$. Use a logits formulation:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\rm{Loss} = - \\sum_i t_i \\, log \\, p_i\n",
        "$$\n",
        "with $p$ given by the the softmax function in terms of the logits $h$:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "p_i = \\frac{\\exp(h_i)}{\\sum_{i'} \\exp(h_{i'})} .\n",
        "$$\n",
        "Inserting $p$ in the expression for the loss gives\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\rm{Loss} = - \\sum_i t_i h_i + \\rm{LogSumExp}(h) \\ ,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "where\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\rm{LogSumExp}(h) = \\log \\sum_i \\exp h_i \\ .\n",
        "$$\n",
        "This is true for $t$ being a one-hot vector.\n",
        "\n",
        "Call the function to convince yourself it works.\n",
        "\n",
        "In practice you want to implement a [numerically stable](https://leimao.github.io/blog/LogSumExp/) version of LogSumExp. But we will not bother about that here.\n",
        "\n",
        "Help: You can add these methods in the Var class:\n",
        "\n",
        "    def exp(self):\n",
        "        return Var(exp(self.v), lambda: [(self, exp(self.v))])\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def log(self):\n",
        "        return Var(log(self.v), lambda: [(self, self.v ** -1)])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 149,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6nMuxyfzFtHv"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Var(v=1.3133, grad=0.0000)\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def cross_entropy_loss(t, h):\n",
        "\n",
        "    Loss = Var(0.0)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # -sum(t[i] * h[i])\n",
        "    for i in range(len(t)):\n",
        "        Loss = Loss - (Var(float(t[i])) * h[i])\n",
        "\n",
        "    # log(sum(exp(h[i])))\n",
        "    sum_exp = Var(0.0)\n",
        "    for i in range(len(h)):\n",
        "        sum_exp = sum_exp + h[i].exp()\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # combining terms\n",
        "    Loss += sum_exp.log()\n",
        "    return Loss\n",
        "\n",
        "# Testing the function:\n",
        "t = [1.0, 0.0]\n",
        "h = [Var(0.0), Var(1.0)]\n",
        "\n",
        "loss = cross_entropy_loss(t, h)\n",
        "print(loss)"
      ]
    },
